  "id": "DrugBank_DB09096 - MONDO_6547",
  "verbalization": "Benzoyl Peroxide is implicated in the pathogenesis of Exanthem (disease) through a chain of indications that link it to Contact Dermatitis and Desoximetasone, both of which are associated with Exanthem. The evidence suggests that Benzoyl Peroxide may act as a mediator in the development of Exanthem by inducing Contact Dermatitis, which in turn is linked to Desoximetasone, a corticosteroid that also contributes to Exanthem. This pathway implies a potential role of Benzoyl Peroxide in exacerbating inflammatory responses through its interaction with dermatological conditions, which may trigger systemic manifestations of Exanthem. The overlapping indications between Benzoyl Peroxide and Exanthem highlight a possible mechanistic link involving inflammatory or allergic responses, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
